   145	- **Internal writes** (ConfigStore commits, consumer checkpoints, maintenance) are `kind: "internal"`.
   146	  They take a position, appear in `cutCatalog`, and appear in `transactions()` as opaque records unless
   147	  `journaled: false`.
   148	
   149	### 2.5 Race groups
   150	
   151	Contiguous commands with the same `race` id. Committed members are replayed in receipt position order
   152	and each must succeed. A rejected member must fail at some serialization point (before, between or after
   153	the committed members); its expected outcome lists `possibleCategories`. A member that would succeed at
   154	every point is a FAIL.
   155	
   156	## 3. Queries
   157	
   158	Every query has `id`, `kind`, and usually a `cut`:
   159	
   160	```jsonc
   161	"cut": {"scope": "s1", "position": 5 | "latest" | {"afterCommand": 3} | {"coordinate": {...}},   // R-CUT-5
   162	        "recordedAt": 1000.25,   // optional R, independent of P
   163	        "validAt": 20.25,        // V; required where the kind reads valid time
   164	        "publicBasis": true}     // false lets self-checks use negative instants
   165	```
